#: lib/ascella_web/controllers/help_html/show.html.heex:84
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "When a newer Ascella is out, the page says so at the top, with an Update Ascella button. It is checked the same way as every other download, and it goes last: Update all does the other programs first, and Ascella refuses to update itself while it is installing, updating or going back for another program. Your data is not touched."
msgstr ""

#: lib/ascella_web/controllers/help_html/show.html.heex:96
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Windows: Ascella closes, its own installer (Velopack) swaps the program, and Ascella starts again. Linux: the update is handed to Ascella's update service, which restarts Ascella and puts the old version back if the new one does not answer."
msgstr ""

#: lib/ascella_web/controllers/help_html/show.html.heex:90
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Mac: Ascella puts the new Ascella.app in place of the old one in the same folder, keeps the old one in a folder called .ascella-previous, quits, and the new one opens by itself. If the new one does not answer within a minute, the old one is put back and opened, and the page tells you. This needs Ascella.app to sit in a folder you may change, such as Applications; if it was opened straight from Downloads, Ascella says so: quit it, drag it into Applications and open it from there. The very first Ascella, if you got it with a browser, still has to be allowed once (right-click, Open; on macOS 15 and newer, Open Anyway in System Settings > Privacy & Security); after that it updates itself."
msgstr ""

